● INNER JOIN:
------------------ 
●Inner join retrive only matched rows.
●In inner-join, we have to specify the condition & only matched rows are considered
 
Inner join state that what data is same on two tables that data only retrieve. Then that is called a inner join.
●It returns dataset that have matching value in both sides
 
   
2.1 Natural Join :
--------------------
It is same as inner-join with 2 differnces
	1.duplicate column will not displayed
	2 .Here we need not specify the condition
Query:
SELECT * 
FROM Employee 
NATURAL JOIN Department;

sA natural join is a type of relational database operation that combines two tables based on matching column names.
It automatically identifies and combines rows from both tables where the column names in both tables are the same, 
without the need for explicitly specifying the join condition. This type of join is used to simplify queries when tables
have similar structures and share common columns, but it can also be risky if column names change or if there are multiple
columns with the same name in the tables.
 


 
 
● LEFT JOIN:
---------------
●It returns all Records from the left table and matched records from the right.
● 
 SELECT * 
FROM Employee 
LEFT JOIN Department 
ON Employee.dept_id = Department.dept_id;

 
● RIGHT JOIN:
--------------
It returns all Records from the right table and the matched records from left.
 
 SELECT * 
FROM Employee 
RIGHT JOIN Department 
ON Employee.dept_id = Department.dept_id;

 
OUTER JOIN
 ---------------
OUTER JOIN in SQL Server returns all records from both tables
 
. In other words, this join will not return only the matching record but also return all unmatched rows from one or both tables.
   
MySQL does not support FULL JOIN directly

SELECT * FROM Employee
LEFT JOIN Department ON Employee.dept_id = Department.dept_id
UNION
SELECT * FROM Employee
RIGHT JOIN Department ON Employee.dept_id = Department.dept_id;

4.Equi Join:
---------------
	In join condition, if we specify = operator then it is called as Equi Join
SELECT * 
FROM Employee, Department 
WHERE Employee.dept_id = Department.dept_id;
	 
 
5.Non-Equi Join:	
---------------
	In join condition, if we specify except = operator(<,>,<=,>=,!=) then it is called as Non-Equi Join
SELECT * 
FROM Employee, Department 
WHERE Employee.dept_id = Department.dept_id;
  
 
6.Self Join
--------------
	If join is performed on single table then it called as Self join
SELF JOIN

A table is joined to itself using the SELF JOIN.
A self join is used to join a table to itself
    
SELECT e1.name AS Employee, e2.name AS Manager
FROM Employee e1, Employee e2
WHERE e1.manager_id = e2.emp_id;

